<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- 17o batch d, ledger row 10 — the "Fill code · From Messages" popover
	     over the note title. On macOS 26 that suggestion is time-and-focus
	     based and content-agnostic: every text-input-capable field in every
	     Mac app is eligible while Messages or Mail has recently detected a
	     one-time code. This key (macOS 26+, default NO) is the one documented
	     opt-out — with it YES, only a field explicitly annotated
	     `.textContentType(.oneTimeCode)` is offered the suggestion.
	     Variorum has no verification-code field, so nothing loses anything;
	     credential AutoFill (.password / .newPassword / .username in the auth
	     views) is a different mechanism and is untouched.

	     THE ONE COST, stated: a one-time-code field added later MUST carry
	     that annotation. `OneTimeCodeAutoFillTests` pins both halves.

	     This file is a PARTIAL plist: GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE stays YES and
	     Xcode merges its generated keys over these, because the
	     INFOPLIST_KEY_* build-setting road only carries key names Xcode
	     itself knows (measured: the setting was silently dropped from the
	     built bundle).

	     It sits BESIDE the synchronized source folder rather than inside
	     it: a plist under `Variorum/` joins that group's Copy Bundle
	     Resources phase automatically and Xcode warns that the target is
	     copying its own Info.plist into Resources. -->
	<key>NSAutoFillRequiresTextContentTypeForOneTimeCodeOnMac</key>
	<true/>
	<!-- Phase 13r U2 — SPARKLE, the update channel (rulings R-13r-1/2/7;
	     the 13r plan's U2 RECORD). Shared by Debug and Release like
	     everything in this file, and INERT in Debug: the updater is
	     instantiated only outside DEBUG (UpdateChannel.swift — R-13r-7's
	     fence), and Sparkle does nothing until something instantiates it.

	     SUPublicEDKey — the PUBLIC half of the EdDSA key the author minted
	     at HER HANDS step 3 (2026-10-04; the private half lives in her login
	     Keychain + ONE password-manager backup, never in or beside this
	     repo). Every appcast enclosure must verify against it.

	     SUFeedURL — THE BAKED URL, ruled and LOCKED (R-13r-2 + the site-side
	     report): stargazing.tech serves it no-cache. The R-13r-8 walk
	     overrides it with a user default on a SCRATCH install only (Sparkle
	     reads a defaults SUFeedURL first); update testing never uses this.

	     SUEnableInstallerLauncherService — REQUIRED for a sandboxed app
	     (Sparkle's sandboxing doc): the installer runs outside the sandbox,
	     launched over XPC; Variorum.entitlements carries the -spks/-spki
	     mach-lookup exceptions it needs. The DOWNLOADER service stays OFF:
	     the app already holds network.client, and Sparkle says not to enable
	     it then.

	     Deliberately ABSENT (each one's absence is a decision):
	     SUEnableAutomaticChecks — so Sparkle's standard consent flow ASKS
	     before any automatic check (on the second launch); SUEnableSystem-
	     Profiling — so no anonymous system profile can ever be sent (no
	     analytics, out loud); SUEnableDownloaderService (above). -->
	<key>SUPublicEDKey</key>
	<string>tn/IQUaJMGk8Q+T8iE3ph2t+xpdzlUDGxg7+k/5xMhA=</string>
	<key>SUFeedURL</key>
	<string>https://stargazing.tech/variorum/appcast.xml</string>
	<key>SUEnableInstallerLauncherService</key>
	<true/>
	<!-- 17y B2, items (a)(b)(e) — THE APP'S OWN DRAG TYPES, DECLARED.
	     Every in-app drag on the Bookcase (a book onto a shelf, a book placed
	     in "my order", a shelf name reordered), in the Book Panel (a note or a
	     chapter moved) and in the sidebar's Open strip (a row reordered) rides
	     a Transferable token whose CodableRepresentation names one of these
	     identifiers via UTType(exportedAs:). An exported type the bundle does
	     NOT declare resolves with no supertypes - it is not public.data - and
	     the system faults at launch ("...was expected to be declared and
	     exported in the Info.plist of Variorum.app, but it was not found");
	     the drag session starts, but no drop site ever accepts the payload:
	     nothing lights, nothing lands (the 17y B2 RECORD's driven
	     reproduction - the cause of 13i-d F-U1-4 / F-U2-4 and of her walk's
	     dead drags). Declared here as plain data, private to this app (no
	     filename extension, no MIME type - they never leave the process).
	     `DragTypeDeclarationTests` pins all three AND scans the sources, so a
	     new `UTType(exportedAs:)` must be declared here or the suite fails. -->
	<key>UTExportedTypeDeclarations</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>UTTypeIdentifier</key>
			<string>io.lduarte.variorum.bookcase-item</string>
			<key>UTTypeDescription</key>
			<string>Variorum Bookcase item</string>
			<key>UTTypeConformsTo</key>
			<array>
				<string>public.data</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>UTTypeIdentifier</key>
			<string>io.lduarte.variorum.book-panel-item</string>
			<key>UTTypeDescription</key>
			<string>Variorum Book Panel item</string>
			<key>UTTypeConformsTo</key>
			<array>
				<string>public.data</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>UTTypeIdentifier</key>
			<string>io.lduarte.variorum.open-note-row</string>
			<key>UTTypeDescription</key>
			<string>Variorum open note</string>
			<key>UTTypeConformsTo</key>
			<array>
				<string>public.data</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
